  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Gilt in the Void",
    "overview": "The table is a set of precious objects hung over deep space. Every panel, board and window is a dark, warm-brown plate in a bevelled gold frame with small corner ornaments. The 3D map shows through the space between them. The look follows the official digital edition of the game: player boards, cards, card backs and pieces come from the official material and are never redrawn or invented. Interface chrome exists only to hold them.\n\nThe system is dense and stays still. A full four-player table shows on one 1920×1080 stage, scaled to the window, so every millimetre is spoken for and nothing scrolls. Gold carries authority: frames, titles, the primary action. Full colour is reserved for game information that the physical game also colours: the seats, the resources, the card suits. Light is a signal: a glow means \"you can use this now\" or \"this is active\", never decoration.\n\nThe old blue-teal interface (blue panels, cyan selection ring, `--panel`, `--rule-hi`, `--select`) is superseded. It survives in early rules of `src/ui/table/table.css` and is to be removed, not extended.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm umber plates in bevelled gold frames with corner ornaments, floating over the starfield and the 3D map.",
      "Official art only: boards, cards, backs and pieces from the game's material; the interface never invents imagery.",
      "Gold for structure and the primary action; saturated colour only for seats, resources and suits.",
      "Glow is a state, not an ornament.",
      "One fixed 1920×1080 stage, scaled to fit: dense, no scrolling, regions computed in one place (`src/ui/table/layout.ts`)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Gold-Is-Structure Rule",
        "body": "Gold draws frames, titles and the single primary action of a group. It never fills a large area, and a group never has two gold-filled buttons.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Game-Colour Rule",
        "body": "Saturated colour on the table always means something in the game: a seat, a resource, a suit, a state. If it means nothing, it is gold, bronze or neutral.",
